------------------------------------------------------------------------
License compatibility
------------------------------------------------------------------------

The plugin source code is Apache-2.0. The vendored third-party headers
are GPL-2.0. When the plugin is compiled, the resulting `ha_stoolap.so`
combines:

  - Apache-2.0 source (this project)
  - GPL-2.0 inline functions and class layouts (vendored wsrep headers
    and MariaDB server-internal headers consumed at compile time)

MariaDB Foundation publishes a "FOSS License Exception" that explicitly
permits Apache-2.0 plugins to link against the GPL-2.0 server. Apache
License 2.0 is on the FOSS Exception's list of permitted licences.

If you redistribute the source tree of this repository, you must:

  - retain this NOTICE file,
  - retain the LICENSE file (Apache 2.0) for the plugin sources,
  - retain the original COPYING / LICENSE files inside
    `third_party/*/`, which carry the GPL-2.0 terms for the vendored
    headers.

If you redistribute the compiled `ha_stoolap.so` together with a
MariaDB binary, the combined work falls under the FOSS License
Exception. Compile-time-only consumption of the GPL-2.0 wsrep headers
is consistent with the headers' redistribution terms.
